WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:01.670
Hello again, SCP Fans!

00:00:01.670 --> 00:00:07.549
We’ve once again sparked up the Anom-O-Tron
6000, our state-of-the-art supercomputer that

00:00:07.549 --> 00:00:12.110
takes countless data streams from the SCP
Foundation’s various anomalies, and allows

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:16.300
us to simulate potential scenarios that could
never normally occur.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:21.950
For example, what if Boba Fett, one of fiction’s
most iconic galactic bounty hunters, took

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:25.140
on the Sarkic menace that is The Flesh That
Hates?

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:26.140
Well…

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:28.000
Let’s press the button and find out!

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:33.000
A long time ago in a barely explored corner
of a galaxy far, far away…

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:38.560
The rhythmic blink of bright red emergency
lights brought the hunter back to consciousness.

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:42.550
Beneath the tinted visor of his helmet, his
vision was still blurry from the blow he had

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:46.440
taken to the head as his ship had jolted to
a stop.

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:50.950
Blinking away the haze clouding his eyesight,
he focused on the light still flashing up

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:54.920
at him from the console in front of the seat
he was strapped into.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:56.100
Wait, was he?

00:00:56.100 --> 00:01:00.530
He lifted a gloved hand to double-check; still
secure, buckled in tight.

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:04.830
Finally able to see again, the bounty hunter
turned to the console, checking the readouts

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:07.160
on the circular screens of his ship’s cockpit.

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:11.440
It didn’t take running a quick diagnostic
for him to realize his predicament.

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:16.580
As durable and heavily armored as his trusty
Firespray was, the vessel had taken a pretty

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:17.790
nasty hit.

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:21.549
He knew he was taking a risk flying through
an area of space controlled by the infamous

00:01:21.549 --> 00:01:22.890
Crimson Dawn.

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:28.230
The crime syndicate maintained a fragile alliance
with the hunter’s slothful, slug-like employer,

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:32.990
but after spotting his ship trying to pass
through their territory undetected, they had

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:33.990
retaliated.

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:39.049
Sending a squad of ships after the Firespray,
and outmaneuvering them hadn’t been easy,

00:01:39.049 --> 00:01:43.400
especially the smaller, single-person fighters
that could zip around at much faster speeds

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.530
than the hunter’s heavy gunship.

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:49.940
But the syndicate had used its fighters as
merely a distraction, drawing his attention

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:53.770
away from the larger attack ship drawing in
from the rear.

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:58.340
Receiving a full blast from an ion cannon
was bad enough; the energy bolt had struck

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:03.330
the hunter’s ship, serving a direct hit
that slowed his vessel down to a crawl, albeit

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:05.350
still intact… for now.

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:10.299
Ion blasts weren’t designed to cause lasting
damage to a ship, only to disrupt all the

00:02:10.299 --> 00:02:11.430
electronic systems on board.

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:16.790
From his cockpit, the bounty hunter knew exactly
why his adversaries had done this; they wanted

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:21.819
to capture him alive, and possibly take his
Firespray too.

00:02:21.819 --> 00:02:26.540
He wasn’t about to let that happen, the
ship had been passed down to him by his father,

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:31.752
along with the armor he now wore, that made
him instantly recognizable as one of the most

00:02:31.752 --> 00:02:33.939
feared hunters in the galaxy.

00:02:33.939 --> 00:02:38.690
But, having his ship rendered without navigation
systems or control over the engines, meant

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:42.690
he couldn’t steer it clear of the path of
an oncoming fighter.

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:46.579
The smaller ship moved to swerve out of the
way, only too late.

00:02:46.579 --> 00:02:50.620
It clipped the Firespray’s wing, causing
the hunter to lurch forward and hit his head

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:55.510
as his ship spun out of control, drifting
away, lost in space.

00:02:55.510 --> 00:02:59.739
By the time he came back around, he found
himself adrift in an unfamiliar, uncharted

00:02:59.739 --> 00:03:01.329
corner of the galaxy.

00:03:01.329 --> 00:03:07.030
His ship was still badly damaged, running
on a reserve of emergency power that was quickly

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:08.030
depleting.

00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:11.419
The hunter fumbled with the controls, taking
a look at the star map on his display.

00:03:11.419 --> 00:03:15.169
He didn’t recognize this quadrant or even
the system he was in.

00:03:15.169 --> 00:03:20.549
There was one planet looming ahead, a green
and blue world with a single neighboring moon…

00:03:20.549 --> 00:03:24.569
It was then the hunter realized what that
red light had been warning him about.

00:03:24.569 --> 00:03:29.159
In its damaged state, the Firespray had been
caught in the planet’s gravitational pull,

00:03:29.159 --> 00:03:32.159
and was now hurtling towards its surface.

00:03:32.159 --> 00:03:37.700
Holding on tight, bracing himself for impact,
Boba Fett prepared for a particularly bumpy

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:38.700
landing.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:42.389
The entire ship buckled as it passed through
the planet’s upper atmosphere, the metalwork

00:03:42.389 --> 00:03:46.139
creaking as scraps were torn away from the
outer hull by the extreme g-force.

00:03:46.139 --> 00:03:51.469
Boba yanked at the steering columns, barely
able to change the course of his ship’s

00:03:51.469 --> 00:03:52.469
descent.

00:03:52.469 --> 00:03:56.900
The power was still minimal after the ion
attack, practically running on fumes.

00:03:56.900 --> 00:04:01.370
Looking out of the large front viewport, Fett
could see streaks of heat as his Firespray

00:04:01.370 --> 00:04:02.999
plummeted to the surface.

00:04:02.999 --> 00:04:06.639
He had an idea, a risky move but it might
just work.

00:04:06.639 --> 00:04:11.900
If it didn’t, then his storied career as
the galaxy’s most infamous bounty hunter

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:16.630
might just come to an unremarkable, anticlimactic
ending.

00:04:16.630 --> 00:04:20.760
Pulling at the controls, he repositioned the
ship’s remaining fin-like wing – the one

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:25.870
still mostly operational – and angled the
Firespray so that its rear boosters were facing

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:30.200
towards the planet, its internal gyro system
keeping him sat upright.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:35.610
Still tumbling straight down, now in landing
position, all Boba could do was hold tight

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:40.560
and pray… prayers that were answered when
the console lit up with an alert.

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:45.570
The heat of re-entry had jumpstarted the engines,
reigniting the gunship’s propulsion system;

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:50.500
not enough for sustained flight, but adequate
to allow the hunter to control his descent,

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:53.112
and lessen the impact of the rough landing.

00:04:53.112 --> 00:04:58.580
The Firespray came to a crashing halt in the
snow, still mostly intact, but too badly damaged

00:04:58.580 --> 00:04:59.840
to take off.

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:03.110
Clambering his way out, Boba Fett examined
the wreckage of his ship.

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:07.710
It had been in far worse scrapes over the
years, but every time the Firespray sustained

00:05:07.710 --> 00:05:13.050
damage, he couldn’t help but think of what
his father, Jango, would say – or his donor,

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:19.340
as some would call him, given that Boba was
a pure, unaltered genetic clone of his ‘dad’.

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:23.380
Turning around, he looked out over the expanse
of the frozen region he’d crashed on.

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:28.210
The wind carried with it an icy bite; Fett
was only shielded from it by the insulated

00:05:28.210 --> 00:05:32.680
flight suit he wore under his green-painted
plates of Beskar steel armor.

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:37.780
He lowered the antenna on his Mandalorian
helmet, using its viewfinder to survey the

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:38.780
horizon.

00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:44.051
Instantly, his eyes spotted a sign, a worn
sheet of metal, half-buried in the snow.

00:05:44.051 --> 00:05:48.900
There was something off about this sign though,
that instantly told Boba he wasn’t on Hoth,

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:53.490
Illum, Orto Plutonia, or any other ice planet
he knew of.

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:58.440
He trudged closer to the sign, crossing the
frozen tundra alone, the cape over his shoulder

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:00.180
whipping in the freezing cold gale.

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:05.170
Where there was a sign, there could easily
be civilization, maybe even somewhere Fett

00:06:05.170 --> 00:06:07.630
could get parts to fix his inherited ship.

00:06:07.630 --> 00:06:12.150
He forced himself not to stop and examine
the sign, but couldn’t help glancing at

00:06:12.150 --> 00:06:13.340
it as he passed.

00:06:13.340 --> 00:06:17.741
Boba couldn’t recognize the lettering written
on it at all, not the characters that had

00:06:17.741 --> 00:06:21.160
been printed on the metal, nor the word painted
over it in red.

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:25.331
At first, he’d thought it might be Aurebesh,
but the closer he got he realized it was a

00:06:25.331 --> 00:06:27.590
language he didn’t understand.

00:06:27.590 --> 00:06:32.250
Continuing on past it, Boba tried to put thoughts
of the sign out of his head, unaware that

00:06:32.250 --> 00:06:37.820
it read ‘Lake Baikal, Siberia’… and
that someone had painted the Russian word

00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:39.210
for ‘Run’ over it.

00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:44.170
It didn’t take long for Boba to reach the
civilization that he was looking for, or what

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:45.890
was left of it anyway.

00:06:45.890 --> 00:06:50.090
The small fishing town reminded him a little
of the city of Mos Espa back on Tattooine,

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:53.670
although it looked to have been abandoned
for quite some time.

00:06:53.670 --> 00:06:57.330
The rickety buildings were all constructed
out of wooden planks, with a thick coating

00:06:57.330 --> 00:07:00.340
of frost over almost every surface.

00:07:00.340 --> 00:07:05.700
As Boba marched further in, a gunslinger walking
into a frozen ghost town, there was almost

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:07.230
total silence.

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:10.400
The cold winds had died down to barely a whisper
now.

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:15.150
The stranded bounty hunter looked around,
finding no signs of anything nearby.

00:07:15.150 --> 00:07:21.570
No spaceport, no Jawas he could trade with,
no townsfolk to ask for directions, no signs

00:07:21.570 --> 00:07:23.440
of life…

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:27.480
Something moved behind him, causing Boba to
instinctively whip around to face it, producing

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:31.960
his EE-3 carbine blaster
with a draw speed rivaled by few of the fastest

00:07:31.960 --> 00:07:33.420
hands in the galaxy.

00:07:33.420 --> 00:07:39.280
His weapon was trained on nothing, whatever
had caused the sound was nowhere to be seen.

00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:43.560
Keeping his gun up and at the ready in one
hand, Boba reached for a button on one of

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:44.700
his gauntlets.

00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:49.930
Within his helmet, the pure white of the snow
blinked away, replaced by a blue filter, providing

00:07:49.930 --> 00:07:53.770
him with a head’s up display that highlighted
any nearby heat signatures.

00:07:53.770 --> 00:07:59.169
There was a trail on the ground just a few
feet from him; not tracks, mind you, just

00:07:59.169 --> 00:08:02.750
a single streak of warmth left carved through
the snow.

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:04.970
Cautiously, Boba followed it.

00:08:04.970 --> 00:08:09.360
The trail curved around a nearby shack, and
then disappeared through a hole that had been

00:08:09.360 --> 00:08:15.250
punched through one of its walls; the wooden
planks it was built from were all splintered

00:08:15.250 --> 00:08:18.290
outwards, as if something large had burst
out of it.

00:08:18.290 --> 00:08:22.870
Inside the shack had been coated in enough
frost to freeze everything solid; cups and

00:08:22.870 --> 00:08:26.560
plates at the dinner table looked like they’d
been encased in carbonite.

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:31.290
Looking around the dark, abandoned interior,
Boba barely noticed something slithering down

00:08:31.290 --> 00:08:33.139
towards him from the ceiling…

00:08:33.139 --> 00:08:37.699
A winding, fleshy appendage whipped around
Boba’s arm, locking it tightly in place.

00:08:37.699 --> 00:08:41.509
He pulled against it with all his strength,
but the bounty hunter couldn’t free his

00:08:41.509 --> 00:08:43.959
hand, or the blaster he was holding.

00:08:43.959 --> 00:08:48.320
Turning to see his attacker through the boards
of the upper floor, Fett could make out a

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:53.980
writhing, massive shadow attached to the long,
grotesque appendage that now had him in an

00:08:53.980 --> 00:08:54.980
armlock.

00:08:54.980 --> 00:08:59.420
In all his years of bounty hunting, he’d
never seen a species like it; whatever it

00:08:59.420 --> 00:09:04.410
was, his Beskar and flight suit were protecting
it from feeling its disgusting, slimy grip

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:05.970
against his skin.

00:09:05.970 --> 00:09:09.579
Although he wasn’t too keen on being held
by this monster for much longer.

00:09:09.579 --> 00:09:14.439
With his free hand, Boba tried to wrench the
tentacle off him, only to feel it snaking

00:09:14.439 --> 00:09:19.329
further and tighter around his arm, bending
it in the opposite direction his elbow was

00:09:19.329 --> 00:09:20.579
meant to bend.

00:09:20.579 --> 00:09:26.499
Boba grunted, stifling a scream under his
helmet as he felt his arm on the verge of

00:09:26.499 --> 00:09:27.499
snapping.

00:09:27.499 --> 00:09:31.029
But the pain brought back reminders of his
lessons, his training under his various mentors

00:09:31.029 --> 00:09:34.899
– his father, Aurra, even old Bane.

00:09:34.899 --> 00:09:39.790
Even with his blaster arm ensnared, a good
bounty hunter was never unarmed.

00:09:39.790 --> 00:09:44.430
Knocking the gauntlet on his free arm against
his leg to activate it, he lifted his first

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:49.720
upwards as a streak of flame erupted from
the Mandalorian vambrace, setting fire to

00:09:49.720 --> 00:09:54.870
the wooden floor above… and the creature,
which shrieked in pain as it caught alight,

00:09:54.870 --> 00:09:56.899
relinquishing its grip.

00:09:56.899 --> 00:10:01.639
Thinking fast, and moving at a speed to match,
Boba leaped out of the way as the huge monster

00:10:01.639 --> 00:10:03.670
came crashing through the burning wood planks.

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:06.589
Had he not rolled to a safe distance just
in time, then it would have landed on him,

00:10:06.589 --> 00:10:11.069
crushing the bounty hunter under its weight.

00:10:11.069 --> 00:10:15.420
Back on his feet, Boba spun on his heel and
opened fire with his now-freed blaster, each

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:19.710
blast of the red laser light illuminating
the horrific sight of what had attacked him.

00:10:19.710 --> 00:10:27.079
It was a mass of flesh, distorted and disfigured,
like a bloated, coagulated wound given form.

00:10:27.079 --> 00:10:31.899
It might once have been a person, but now
extra legs had sprouted beneath it, arms having

00:10:31.899 --> 00:10:37.290
melted into slimy, blood-red tendrils that
were flailing in pain as the creature tried

00:10:37.290 --> 00:10:39.070
to douse the fire.

00:10:39.070 --> 00:10:43.410
Boba backed out of the shack’s front entrance,
still firing his carbine blaster.

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:48.230
Its bolts were having little effect on the
fleshy, inhuman monster, seeming to only cause

00:10:48.230 --> 00:10:52.120
it irritation rather than leaving any lasting
damage.

00:10:52.120 --> 00:10:57.619
But as the infamous hunter moved his foot
behind him, a wooden porch step snapped beneath,

00:10:57.619 --> 00:11:00.699
causing him to topple over, landing on his
back in the snow.

00:11:00.699 --> 00:11:05.199
His blaster had fallen from his hands as he
came crashing down, forcing him to roll over

00:11:05.199 --> 00:11:06.220
and reach for it.

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:09.160
That’s when he saw the others…

00:11:09.160 --> 00:11:13.759
Emerging from the abandoned, rural town, a
group of nightmarish abominations were slithering

00:11:13.759 --> 00:11:15.680
out of nearby shacks.

00:11:15.680 --> 00:11:20.800
They shambled towards Boba, each one of them
looking different from the next, but no less

00:11:20.800 --> 00:11:24.639
stomach-churning in their fleshy, blood-soaked
appearances.

00:11:24.639 --> 00:11:29.709
Some were bipedal, walking on the remnants
of two legs, but with their entire upper body

00:11:29.709 --> 00:11:33.050
fused into a single, monstrous mass.

00:11:33.050 --> 00:11:37.579
Others looked like they had once been small
animals, but had been cruelly and unnaturally

00:11:37.579 --> 00:11:42.310
twisted into amorphous, slimy mutations of
their former selves.

00:11:42.310 --> 00:11:48.060
The horde of beings, a veritable smorgasbord
of Flesh That Hates, were crawling towards

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:49.060
Boba.

00:11:49.060 --> 00:11:53.839
He had spent the earliest parts of his childhood
surrounded by cloners on Kamino, alien experts

00:11:53.839 --> 00:11:55.140
in genetics.

00:11:55.140 --> 00:11:59.410
Since then, he’d been all over the galaxy,
and met people of all different species.

00:11:59.410 --> 00:12:04.290
It wasn’t hard for Boba to see what these
things, these monsters, were.

00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:09.139
They were the townsfolk that lived in this
snow-covered place.

00:12:09.139 --> 00:12:12.820
Or, at least, they used to be people.

00:12:12.820 --> 00:12:14.660
Now they were horrific.

00:12:14.660 --> 00:12:19.230
From behind him, the first creature – the
one that had drawn him out – re-emerged,

00:12:19.230 --> 00:12:20.230
still enraged.

00:12:20.230 --> 00:12:25.119
But, as he turned to look at it, making sure
he was aware of all threats surrounding him,

00:12:25.119 --> 00:12:26.829
Boba spotted its skin.

00:12:26.829 --> 00:12:31.279
The parts where he had singed it with his
flamethrower were still severely burned, practically

00:12:31.279 --> 00:12:33.100
reduced to a cinder.

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:34.100
Fire.

00:12:34.100 --> 00:12:35.850
That could hurt them.

00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:40.160
Reaching to the ground to retrieve and stow
his blaster, Boba felt something tugging at

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:43.509
the weapon, pulling it in the opposite direction.

00:12:43.509 --> 00:12:47.690
Another of the fleshy monsters, a crawling,
spider-like collection of arms and legs with

00:12:47.690 --> 00:12:53.550
no body or head, had flung an appendage outwards
and grabbed the carbine.

00:12:53.550 --> 00:12:57.730
Trying to pull it back, Boba slipped in the
snow, and was being dragged towards the writhing

00:12:57.730 --> 00:12:58.940
monstrosity.

00:12:58.940 --> 00:13:03.899
A loud bang echoed around the nearby town,
punctuated by a bright, red light soaring

00:13:03.899 --> 00:13:08.110
through the sky and gently floating back down
towards the ground.

00:13:08.110 --> 00:13:12.490
The white-hot flare filled the area with a
glow, the creatures all momentarily turning

00:13:12.490 --> 00:13:15.660
their attention to it, sensing its heat.

00:13:15.660 --> 00:13:20.390
That split second was his one chance, all
of Boba’s instincts, every lesson Jango

00:13:20.390 --> 00:13:25.759
had taught him, told him to strike first if
he wanted to make it away alive.

00:13:25.759 --> 00:13:29.529
He dropped the blaster, leaving it in the
creature’s grip – he had spares back on

00:13:29.529 --> 00:13:33.519
the Firespray, but they’d be no good to
him if he was dead.

00:13:33.519 --> 00:13:38.290
Hitting one of the tiny switches on his vambrace,
two scorching hot flames spat from the exhausts

00:13:38.290 --> 00:13:39.939
of Boba’s jetpack.

00:13:39.939 --> 00:13:44.181
Immediately, he was lifted up off the ground,
hovering just above the roofs of the small

00:13:44.181 --> 00:13:46.170
wooden structures around him.

00:13:46.170 --> 00:13:50.110
In that same microsecond, the abominations
of flesh turned their collective attention

00:13:50.110 --> 00:13:52.179
back to their airborne prey.

00:13:52.179 --> 00:13:57.230
The ones that still had heads, or had grown
extra, disfigured, and misshapen growths in

00:13:57.230 --> 00:14:02.769
place of a head, looked up at Boba; to them,
he was merely another vessel for them to infect

00:14:02.769 --> 00:14:04.860
with the same disease that plagued them.

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:11.319
But little did any of them know, he was the
Boba Fett, the galaxy’s deadliest, most

00:14:11.319 --> 00:14:16.329
infamous, Beskar-clad bounty hunter – and
a good bounty hunter was never unarmed.

00:14:16.329 --> 00:14:21.040
Igniting in an instant, the flickering nozzle
end of Boba’s wrist-mounted flamethrower

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:25.499
began spraying super-heated fuel over the
horde of monstrosities below.

00:14:25.499 --> 00:14:30.149
Long tongues of orange flame engulfed the
writhing, slithering creatures, burning them

00:14:30.149 --> 00:14:35.949
to a crisp as Boba Fett rained unrelenting
hell down on the Flesh That Hates.

00:14:35.949 --> 00:14:39.910
Hovering above them, he had given himself
enough high ground to gain an advantage.

00:14:39.910 --> 00:14:43.920
Ironically, the distance Boba had to put between
himself and the monsters wasn’t dissimilar

00:14:43.920 --> 00:14:48.990
to the detachment he had for those he had
killed or captured for Jabba the Hutt in the

00:14:48.990 --> 00:14:49.990
past.

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:55.180
They had all been people too, just like these
twisted masses of flesh had once been human.

00:14:55.180 --> 00:14:59.399
Pushing those thoughts down, like he’d been
taught to, Boba’s attention was focused

00:14:59.399 --> 00:15:03.860
on blasting any of the fleeing creatures,
burning them with enough intensity to leave

00:15:03.860 --> 00:15:06.589
little behind but charred remains.

00:15:06.589 --> 00:15:10.779
Except he had forgotten, in his haste, to
check behind him.

00:15:10.779 --> 00:15:14.939
The monster that had first attacked him was
making quick work of scaling the nearest single-story

00:15:14.939 --> 00:15:18.009
shack, and flailed one of its appendages at
Boba.

00:15:18.009 --> 00:15:22.300
It caught him in mid-air, plucking him out
of the sky and wrenching him back down to

00:15:22.300 --> 00:15:24.420
the snowy ground once more.

00:15:24.420 --> 00:15:28.339
Winded, Boba was gasping to catch his breath
underneath his helmet.

00:15:28.339 --> 00:15:32.220
He certainly didn’t need to look to know
his jetpack had most likely been damaged by

00:15:32.220 --> 00:15:33.220
his fall.

00:15:33.220 --> 00:15:35.980
But that was currently the least of his worries.

00:15:35.980 --> 00:15:41.490
Towering above, looming over him, the repulsive
monster looked like it was rearing up to pounce.

00:15:41.490 --> 00:15:46.139
Boba reached to relight his flamethrower,
only for his gauntlet to spark; it had taken

00:15:46.139 --> 00:15:47.839
a hit on the way down too.

00:15:47.839 --> 00:15:52.509
Desperation set it, he lifted his knee and
fired two darts from the micro cannons mounted

00:15:52.509 --> 00:15:54.179
on his yellow kneepads.

00:15:54.179 --> 00:15:58.170
The spiked darts became embedded in the fleshy
creature’s mass, barely fazing it.

00:15:58.170 --> 00:16:03.160
Loading a wrist rocket, Boba raised his other
vambrace to fire, only for the arm he wore

00:16:03.160 --> 00:16:07.980
it on to be grabbed by one of the other creatures,
still-burning, half-alive.

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:10.660
Meanwhile, the one on the roof looked ready
to leap.

00:16:10.660 --> 00:16:15.339
It sprung into the air, ready to come crashing
down to kill the feared former bounty hunter.

00:16:15.339 --> 00:16:20.180
A bright light burst from somewhere nearby;
it wasn’t another flare, this one was a

00:16:20.180 --> 00:16:22.949
blinding eruption of pure white.

00:16:22.949 --> 00:16:27.790
Even through the tinted T-shaped visor of
his helmet, it stung Boba’s eyes so much

00:16:27.790 --> 00:16:30.100
that he had to cover his face with his hand.

00:16:30.100 --> 00:16:34.730
As he peered back, he almost mistook the light
grey of the sky for the same light.

00:16:34.730 --> 00:16:36.819
Looking around, the monster had vanished.

00:16:36.819 --> 00:16:40.839
Those that were left were still writhing,
their amorphous bodies coated with fire, which

00:16:40.839 --> 00:16:43.980
was rapidly spreading to the wood of the nearby
houses.

00:16:43.980 --> 00:16:47.949
Keeping his guard up, as he always did, Boba
climbed to his feet, lifting the gauntlet

00:16:47.949 --> 00:16:50.739
with a miniature blaster mounted on it to
defend himself.

00:16:50.739 --> 00:16:55.439
He’d seen, and even used, disintegration
weapons in the past, but the bounty hunter

00:16:55.439 --> 00:17:00.569
had never known anything to make a creature
like that monster completely vanish in a single

00:17:00.569 --> 00:17:01.569
flash.

00:17:01.569 --> 00:17:06.579
He turned at a sound, not one of the creatures
or the gentle crackling of flames, but the

00:17:06.579 --> 00:17:09.980
gentle crunch of snow under someone’s foot.

00:17:09.980 --> 00:17:14.030
Three strangers walked slowly up to Boba,
not one among them flinching when he lifted

00:17:14.030 --> 00:17:15.960
his vambrace, standing his ground.

00:17:15.960 --> 00:17:20.839
Their clothing was patchwork, cobbled together
from scraps, but looked similar to the same

00:17:20.839 --> 00:17:23.170
cloaks worn by the Jedi of old.

00:17:23.170 --> 00:17:27.650
As the group approached him, the bounty hunter
noticed their bodies had also been altered,

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:31.650
although not in the same way as the vile,
fleshy creatures that now littered the snow

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:32.850
around him.

00:17:32.850 --> 00:17:37.550
Metalwork, mechanized components, and devices
of all manner protruded from their uncovered

00:17:37.550 --> 00:17:43.280
arms and necks, pieces of machinery embedded
in their skulls in the place of their eyes.

00:17:43.280 --> 00:17:48.260
Boba was no stranger to cyborgs, those who
had modified their own bodies with technological

00:17:48.260 --> 00:17:50.820
augmentations and modifications.

00:17:50.820 --> 00:17:55.510
One of the three was missing an entire hand,
in its place was what looked to be some kind

00:17:55.510 --> 00:17:58.640
of cannon, still warm from having just fired.

00:17:58.640 --> 00:18:03.560
The cloaked, mechanized trio looked at Fett
with curiosity, as if they were examining…

00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:06.400
no, admiring his armor.

00:18:06.400 --> 00:18:10.320
Just like his damaged ship, Boba’s armor
belonged to his father, and if these three

00:18:10.320 --> 00:18:12.940
wanted to take it, they’d have to kill him
for it.

00:18:12.940 --> 00:18:17.290
“I take it that was your flare that distracted
them?” he growled beneath his helmet.

00:18:17.290 --> 00:18:22.380
The frontmost of the group nodded, bowing
his head gently, indicating he meant no harm.

00:18:22.380 --> 00:18:23.380
“Indeed.

00:18:23.380 --> 00:18:28.410
We saw something, a vessel, we believe, fall
from the sky not far from here,” the part-man,

00:18:28.410 --> 00:18:29.670
part-machine replied.

00:18:29.670 --> 00:18:32.440
“Was that your craft, warrior?”

00:18:32.440 --> 00:18:34.760
Lowering his arm at last, Boba nodded in response.

00:18:34.760 --> 00:18:38.080
“Don’t suppose you know where I can get
my ship fixed?”

00:18:38.080 --> 00:18:39.080
the hunter asked.

00:18:39.080 --> 00:18:42.840
“We may be able to assist you,” one of
the other two interjected.

00:18:42.840 --> 00:18:45.860
“You have machinery, we watched you use
it to fight.

00:18:45.860 --> 00:18:47.160
Are you one of us?”

00:18:47.160 --> 00:18:52.400
“I give my allegiance to no one,” Boba
stated as he eyed the speaker; he barely looked

00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:54.420
older than a teenager.

00:18:54.420 --> 00:18:55.720
“Who are you people?”

00:18:55.720 --> 00:19:00.570
“Some have called us Mekhanites, others
know us as the Church of the Broken God,”

00:19:00.570 --> 00:19:02.310
the leader spoke up in reply.

00:19:02.310 --> 00:19:05.920
“Little of that matters now, not since the
Flesh overran this place.

00:19:05.920 --> 00:19:13.360
They spread via skin contact, only the parts
of our bodies we have yet to mechanize are

00:19:13.360 --> 00:19:14.560
still vulnerable to their infection.

00:19:14.560 --> 00:19:16.790
I certainly hope none of them touched you,
warrior.”

00:19:16.790 --> 00:19:20.740
Boba took a look over his shoulder at the
bodies of the still-burning creatures, glad

00:19:20.740 --> 00:19:24.980
that his helmet was pressurized and his flight
suit was on tight.

00:19:24.980 --> 00:19:26.840
“The Flesh,” he muttered to himself.

00:19:26.840 --> 00:19:29.340
“I’m fine,” he declared with certainty.

00:19:29.340 --> 00:19:32.140
“In that case,” the lead Mekhanite said.

00:19:32.140 --> 00:19:35.170
“Let’s see about fixing your ship, shall
we?”

00:19:35.170 --> 00:19:44.100
Now go and check out “SCP-096 vs SCP-343”
and “SCP-049 vs SCP-173” if you want to

00:19:44.100 --> 00:19:49.290
hear about the outcomes of more chaotic clashes
between anomalies battling each other for

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:49.700
supremacy!

